	(text "Host USB-C port of the hub (spec sections 3a, 3b). KTS1693: external OVLO 100k / 26.4k 0.1 % (E192) trips at 5.56-5.93 V: above a legal 5.5 V VBUS,\nbelow the USBLC6's 6 V breakdown (the internal threshold, 5.77-6.13 V, is not).\nISET 2.87k -> limit 3.17 / 3.48 / 3.80 A (10000 / R, +/-9 %, 0-70 C): a 3 A host is not cut off; the cable header's 3 x 1 A contacts are the 3 A limit.\nEN tied low. OC_MODE open: the internal 5 M pull-up makes it high = auto-restart (limits for 8 ms, off, retries after 200 ms).\nACOK is open-drain and not used by the hub (J_USB pin 8 is open there). CDET unused. D504 (TVS2200 on connector VBUS) is a DNP footprint.\nUSBLC6-2SC6 VBUS (pin 5) is on VBUS_LOCAL, never on connector VBUS.\nCC1/CC2: 5.1k Rd (0805 for a 20 V CC short) and TVS2200 (22 V VRWM); hub-conn adds 100k in series before the Pico's ADC pins.\nJ_USB is reversal-safe: an end-reversed cable keeps VBUS on VBUS and GND on GND; D+/D- swap and USB does not enumerate."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
